 Caldria.\n  - Norvane Utilities plans 2027 spending up 12%.\n  - Both plans are mostly substations and transformers.\n  - Pellham has a transformer tender of about C$900M due to award in Q1 2027. Norvane has a C$450M tender in Q2.\n  - VLTX holdings won 60% of the last tender round. That 60% is a track record and does not guarantee a share of these tenders.\n- **Data centres:**\n  - Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027. That is slower than 2026, because power availability limits new sites.\n  - The connection queue grew 4% in Q3 2026. Data centres are 60% of new requests, and the average wait is 26 months.\n  - Demand is therefore growing, but at a slowing rate, and long waits can push when the equipment is actually bought.\n- **Order trend:** VLTX holdings' utility order intake rose each quarter, from C$610M in 2025Q4 to C$640M, C$655M and C$670M in 2026Q1 to Q3.\n\n**Risk:** The plans are not yet funded. Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Two utility share offerings were cut back in Q3. Pellham was put on negative watch after its withdrawn offering. If financing is tight, the 18% rise at Pellham, the largest buyer, could slip or be delayed. That is the main risk to this conclusion. Node n3 is working on the financing question.\n\nI did not find a document giving each buyer's weight in VLTX orders (the \"VLTX customer mix\"). I therefore have not sized how much of VLTX's revenue sits with Pellham.","ttft_ms":1632,"type":"result","duration_ms":40147,"uuid":"4e38b2cb-0f49-4473-ba8b-400ccec69479","ttft_stream_ms":984,"time_to_request_ms":65,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":3,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":7,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":15,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":7,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schem